 house with  some slightly different slanted roofs I  think for me slanting your roof slightly  different for every single building is  something that gets kind of annoying  over time but it definitely is really  rewarding since it's one of those very  minut differences which still makes you  like recognize that certain buildings  are different rather than getting the  same pitch in the roof for every damn  building  so yeah I'm mostly using these custom  placeable roofs here just to make sure  that the pitch if the roof is slightly  different for every building and then  there is the D beams that hold up the  roof which you see in a lot of Alpine  architecture throughout Europe which are  just so typical that I want an at least  one building where you've got a lot of  these beams and finally and this is  really become something that I'm almost  over using in the Jaeger horn build I am  placing the small spire if you can call  it that in the front of the building  with the gable decorations by placing  all of these beams in the front and a  vertical wooden post now if I remember  correctly I think there is going to be a  small stall in this building that's why  there should be a tiny door I was  spending way too long trying to get the  right parasols but I just ended up going  with these in the end but yeah there we  go there's a little shop definitely  wanted to make sure that most of the the  shops and stuff like that is going to be  in this one big building here  if I could I probably would have made  this an actual restaurant that would  have been a perfect space for it but  with plenty coastal limitations a small  stall is just about everything that I  can get in there but you know the idea  is still more or less the same this is a  big row of facades which kind of sets  the mood as a village but at the same  time it's a single building with most of  the important facilities in the park  which I didn't have so far because to be  very honest I always forget about  placing toilets and stalls in my parks  so I'm glad at least this time I was on  time to have these kind of things  oh and I guess there's also a little bit  of a mother in touch in the fact that  there's a lot of glass on the upper  floor as well and yeah here we go  bunch of decorations again just to make  everything look a little bit fancy I  suppose maybe it's a little bit too  fancy but you know it's a theme park  besides I do like the way that this  looks I don't think many theme parks  would do this kind of thing think for  theme park realism it's a little bit  over the top but to be perfectly honest  like I said I just like the way that  this looks so there's decorations  everywhere just deal with it I guess  and I think at this point it's more or  less done it's just a little bit of  clutter that I wanted to add here and  there and I do have to say the facade is  not entirely finished yet but finishing  some of the remaining stuff that I still  need to do is gonna be part of the next  episode in which I will have an overview  of what it looks like in the finished  products but for now I'm actually not  going to show you very much of that yet  it's not entirely finished yet and we'll  get to finishing up this whole row of  buildings in the next episode including  the backstage areas so yeah thanks for  watching and I hope to see you guys next  time  [Music]  you
 

